  "worked_solution": "To plot the given function, we follow these steps:\n\n- We take the curve $y=\\left(\\dfrac{1}{5}\\right)^{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14228213/assets/d67114a9865ca54cdf14798e779cfa9c00e71598ba652d6fccdcf686f86e20ef.png)\n\n \n\n- Reflect it on the $x$-axis to give $y=-\\left(\\dfrac{1}{5}\\right)^{x}.$ The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(0,-1)$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14228213/assets/d6dcae76f7fe89188ef449c817f7e7af48c25763077d1daee9626d2f26b1a78a.png)\n\n- Then, vertically shift it by $4$ units up to give $y=-\\left(\\dfrac{1}{5}\\right)^{x}+4.$ The point $(0,-1)$ moves to $(0,3)$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=4.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14228213/assets/529dfc1ef1bc6f0ff58addca6cf27c5039a6cf18c5a307c06a153a3d56040ede.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-317294\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>To plot the given function, we follow these steps:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>We take the curve $y=\\left(\\dfrac{1}{5}\\right)^{x}.$</li>\n</ul>\n<div id=\"graphic-c920915251073985f9ac2e5450b86cf8\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/c920915251073985f9ac2e5450b86cf8\"></div> \n\n<ul>\n<li>Reflect it on the $x$-axis to give $y=-\\left(\\dfrac{1}{5}\\right)^{x}.$ The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(0,-1)$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$</li>\n</ul>\n<div id=\"graphic-a91fb0999d76bcc4b975d02e210c6050\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/a91fb0999d76bcc4b975d02e210c6050\"></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Then, vertically shift it by $4$ units up to give $y=-\\left(\\dfrac{1}{5}\\right)^{x}+4.$ The point $(0,-1)$ moves to $(0,3)$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=4.$</li>\n</ul>\n<div id=\"graphic-eaf42772fd271432f5ca61e1351bf264\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/eaf42772fd271432f5ca61e1351bf264\"></div></div>",
